cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software in academic work, please cite it as below."
title: "AS2 Track Harness (DeepSeek × VLX): asynchronous VLA waypoints fused with a one-plan-per-task VLM planner"
abstract: >-
  An asynchronous navigation harness for a Unitree AS2 quadruped. A fast
  VLX-Go policy supplies 8x3 body-frame waypoints at camera rate; a slow DeepSeek
  planner is asked exactly once per task, before departure, for a ground route
  in the image. The harness fuses the frozen plan with the current VLX path,
  enforces bounded command, telemetry, watchdog and control-lease gates, and
  publishes a read-only observation dashboard. Execution is disabled by default.
type: software
authors:
  - name: "AS2 Track Harness contributors"
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-11-13
license: Apache-2.0
keywords:
  - robotics
  - navigation
  - vision-language-action
  - vision-language-model
  - quadruped
